      "control_name": "Service Access Must Use Short-Lived Credentials",
      "control_description": "Service-to-service access must use short-lived credentials (STS temporary tokens, IAM Roles Anywhere certificates, OIDC federation) rather than long-lived access keys. Short-lived credentials limit the blast radius of compromise — a stolen token expires automatically. This is a core Zero Trust principle: never trust a credential longer than necessary.\n",
